+
+# Threat model: cerbo-supplement-store
+
+This page lists who could attack the app, what they would try, what stops them, and which test proves it.
+Every defence points at a file and line. Every proof points at an acceptance test (AT id) or, where no AT
+exists, a unit test. A row with no test says "⚠ no test". Anything the repo does not contain says "⚠ not built".
+People in the examples are the synthetic demo users (Ana and Ben are patients, Dr. Chen and Dr. Lee are
+providers, Omar, Fran, Dana and Sam are operations staff; all on example.test).
+
+## Trust boundaries
+
+From `docs/architecture/hld.md` §5 (TB-1 to TB-5).
+
+| Id | Boundary | Less trusted side | What guards the crossing |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| TB-1 | Internet → web app | any browser, signed in or not | session check `requireViewer` (`server/services/session.ts:204`), security headers (`nuxt.config.ts:13`), JSON-only bodies (`server/utils/problem.ts:50`) |
+| TB-2 | Between roles inside the app | a signed-in person of one role | BE-4 AccessPolicy, one place, deny by default (`server/services/access-policy.ts:16`) |
+| TB-3 | Web app → database | app code, which can have bugs | the app's database user `supplements_app` gets narrow grants; CHECK constraints and triggers guard money (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:6`, :17, :76, :104) |
+| TB-4 | Web app → outside providers | payment and messaging providers (stubs today) | in-process stubs (`server/services/payment-gateway.ts:34`, `server/services/messaging.ts:15`) |
+| TB-5 | Host platform → our system | the host account and its secret store | outside the repo: ⚠ not built here (CHECKLIST N3) |
+
+## Threats
+
+STRIDE: S spoofing, T tampering, R repudiation, I information disclosure, D denial of service, E elevation of privilege.
+
+| Id | STRIDE | Boundary | Attacker and goal | Attack | Defence (file:line) | Proving test | Residual risk |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| T-1 | I | TB-2 | Ben (patient) wants to read Ana's order | Open another patient's order: change the number in `/api/orders/{id}` | `assertCanViewOrder` lets in only the order's own patient or a provider of its practice; unknown and forbidden both answer not-found (`server/services/access-policy.ts:22`); checked before any read of lines or any write (`server/services/orders.ts:311`). The patient list is scoped to her own id from the session (`server/services/orders.ts:423`, CHECKLIST CK-03) | M4_AT_007 (`tests/acceptance/M4/pay-order.test.ts:85`); M6.1_AT_001 (`tests/acceptance/M6.1/patient-orders.test.ts:25`) | low. Order ids are sequential (`db/migrations/1760000001000_core-orders.sql:59`), so guessing is easy; the check is what holds |
+| T-2 | I | TB-2 | Dr. Lee (other practice) wants Willow Creek orders | Open another practice's order or dashboard by id | same check, practice branch (`server/services/access-policy.ts:25`); orders tied to one practice by composite foreign keys (`db/migrations/1760000001000_core-orders.sql:74`, LINV-3) | M4_AT_008 (`tests/acceptance/M4/pay-order.test.ts:98`); M5_AT_026 (`tests/acceptance/M5/stock-dashboard.test.ts:223`) | low |
+| T-3 | E | TB-2 | Ben wants to act on Ana's order | Start checkout on, or pay, another patient's order | `assertIsOrderPatient` (`server/services/access-policy.ts:41`), called under the order row lock in pay (`server/services/payments.ts:110`) and checkout (`server/services/orders.ts:147`) | M4_AT_043 (`tests/acceptance/M4/pay-order.test.ts:107`) | low |
+| T-4 | E | TB-2 | Dr. Lee wants to send or cancel orders for Willow Creek patients | Send an order for another practice's patient; cancel another practice's order | `assertCanActOnPatient` (`server/services/access-policy.ts:30`, used at `server/services/orders.ts:39`); cancel checks view rights (`server/services/orders.ts:354`); DB composite FKs as backup (`db/migrations/1760000001000_core-orders.sql:74`) | M4_AT_022 (`tests/acceptance/M4/send-order.test.ts:133`); M4_AT_044 (`tests/acceptance/M4/send-order.test.ts:223`) | low |
+| T-5 | T | TB-1 | a patient or provider wants to pay less | Tamper the price in the request: add `unit_price_cents` or an amount to the send or pay body | The send body is a strict schema with only `patient_id`, `product_id`, `quantity`; any extra field is refused (`server/api/orders/index.post.ts:11`). Prices come from the practice's own records (`server/services/orders.ts:68`). Pay reads no body at all, only the order id (`server/api/orders/[orderId]/payments.post.ts:14`), and charges the held prices from the database (`server/services/payments.ts:124`) | server-computed totals: M4_AT_001 (`tests/acceptance/M4/send-order.test.ts:17`). ⚠ no test sends a forged price field | low. The forged-field refusal is untested |
+| T-6 | T | TB-1 | a patient wants the old, lower price after a price rise, or a provider raises the price mid-checkout | Change the price during checkout | Prices are copied onto the lines when checkout starts (`server/services/orders.ts:168`); pay reads only those (`server/services/payments.ts:124`); hold must be live (`server/services/payments.ts:114`); INV-8 | M5_AT_006 (`tests/acceptance/M5/prices.test.ts:125`); M5_AT_042 hold ended (`tests/acceptance/M5/close-out.test.ts:99`) | low |
+| T-7 | T | TB-1, TB-3 | a patient (or a bug) wants to be charged once but get two orders' worth, or a double-click charges twice | Pay twice in parallel with two different keys | Order row lock (`server/services/payments.ts:107`); at most one processing and one succeeded attempt per order, unique indexes (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:54`, :55); INV-2, LINV-6 | M4_AT_038 (`tests/acceptance/M4/pay-order.test.ts:120`) | low |
+| T-8 | T | TB-1 | anyone with a captured request wants a second charge or a confusing state | Replay a payment: resend the same request with the same Idempotency-Key | Key required (`server/services/idempotency.ts:43`); stored per user and key, and a repeat gets the first answer back (`server/services/idempotency.ts:51`, :117); unique `(order_id, idempotency_key)` (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:52`). A replay is not counted against the rate limit (`server/api/orders/[orderId]/payments.post.ts:14`) | M4_AT_006 (`tests/acceptance/M4/pay-order.test.ts:41`); M4_AT_013 (`tests/acceptance/M4/pay-order.test.ts:64`) | low. Keys live 24 hours (`server/services/idempotency.ts:53`); after that, a replay meets a paid order and is refused by T-7's indexes |
+| T-9 | T | TB-3 | someone holding the app's database login (a bug, SQL injection, a leaked app password) wants to rewrite money | Edit the ledger via the app login: UPDATE or DELETE `ledger_entries`, or change a paid order's amounts | The app user may only SELECT and INSERT ledger rows (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:105`); paid orders and their lines are frozen by triggers (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:28`, :39); a succeeded payment attempt is frozen (`db/migrations/1760000003000_idempotency-keys.sql:32`); ledger must balance at commit (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:100`); no DELETE grant on orders (`db/migrations/1760000001000_core-orders.sql:118`). INV-4, LINV-2 | M4_AT_026 (`tests/acceptance/M4/audit-order.test.ts:111`); M4_AT_027 (`tests/acceptance/M4/audit-order.test.ts:129`); M4_AT_030 (`tests/acceptance/M4/audit-order.test.ts:160`) | med. The owner role (`supplements_owner`) can still change anything. That the live database runs the app as `supplements_app` with exactly these grants is not checked (CHECKLIST N10) |
+| T-10 | T | TB-3 | a code bug wants (by accident) to record a split that does not add up | Write a paid order whose item cost + payout + fee ≠ amount paid, or a negative payout | `ck_orders_split_balances` and `ck_orders_payout_nonneg` (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:10`, :12); split checked before charging (`server/services/payments.ts:134`); INV-1, INV-6 | M4_AT_029 (`tests/acceptance/M4/audit-order.test.ts:144`); M5_AT_033 (`tests/acceptance/M5/m4-regressions.test.ts:69`) | low |
+| T-11 | R, T | TB-3 | a provider, Omar or Sam wants to deny or hide a change | Edit or delete price history, stock history or the access log | INSERT and SELECT only: `price_changes` (`db/migrations/1760000012000_price-changes.sql:22`), `stock_movements` (`db/migrations/1760000013000_stock-movements.sql:26`), `access_log` (`db/migrations/1760000014000_operations-access.sql:39`); each row records who and why; INV-4 | M5_AT_004 (`tests/acceptance/M5/prices.test.ts:78`); M5_AT_044 (`tests/acceptance/M5/stock-dashboard.test.ts:321`); M6_AT_027 (`tests/acceptance/M6/roles.test.ts:162`) | low. Same owner-role and live-grant caveat as T-9 (N10) |
+| T-12 | T | TB-1, TB-3 | two patients want the last bottle | Oversell the last unit: pay for it at the same moment | Products locked in id order before the count is checked (`server/services/stock.ts:32`, :50); `ck_products_stock_nonneg` (`db/migrations/1760000001000_core-orders.sql:45`); a short order rolls back with no charge (`server/services/stock.ts:56`); INV-5 | M5_AT_016 (`tests/acceptance/M5/stock-dashboard.test.ts:66`); M5_AT_038 (`tests/acceptance/M5/stock-dashboard.test.ts:277`); M5_AT_015 (`tests/acceptance/M5/stock-dashboard.test.ts:54`) | low |
+| T-13 | I | TB-2 | a curious patient wants to learn the practice's margin or the platform's fee | Cost/fee leak to a patient: read cost, payout or fee from the order view or the receipt | The patient order view returns only lines, prices and total (`server/services/orders.ts:327`); the receipt type has no cost, payout or fee field (`server/services/payments.ts:15`); the catalog with cost is provider-only (`server/api/patients/[patientId]/catalog.get.ts:10`); breakdowns are reviewer-only (`server/api/ops/orders/[orderId].get.ts:11`) | M4_AT_004 checks what the patient sees (`tests/acceptance/M4/send-order.test.ts:74`). ⚠ no test asserts that cost, payout or fee are absent | low. A later field added to the view would leak silently |
+| T-14 | S | TB-1 | an attacker wants to act as Ana | Session theft: steal the cookie (script, network, shared computer) or reuse an old one | Random 32-byte token (`server/services/session.ts:146`), stored only as a SHA-256 hash (`server/services/session.ts:33`, :150); cookie HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax (`server/services/session.ts:196`); idle 15 minutes and absolute 12 hours (`server/services/session.ts:23`, :24, :158); CSP with no inline script (`nuxt.config.ts:14`); HSTS (`nuxt.config.ts:25`); no-store on API and order pages (`nuxt.config.ts:43`); role re-read every request (`server/services/session.ts:180`) | M4_AT_034 (`tests/acceptance/M4/sign-in.test.ts:52`); M6_AT_028 (`tests/acceptance/M6/roles.test.ts:172`); unit: absolute lifetime (`tests/unit/hardening.test.ts:101`), sign-out (`tests/unit/session.test.ts:273`) | low. No second factor (HLD TH-1, A-12). `/` is not no-store (SEC-15, D82). Live headers unchecked (N1) |
