+| T-21 | E | TB-2 | a patient or the wrong staff member wants to change a price or a stock count | Call the price PUT or stock adjustment directly | Price change is provider-only (`server/api/practice/prices/[productId].put.ts:12`), scoped to the provider's practice; stock adjustment is operations-specialist-only (`server/api/ops/stock/[productId]/adjustments.post.ts:12`); stale-count and below-zero refusals (`server/services/stock-adjustments.ts:47`, :51) | M5_AT_009 (`tests/acceptance/M5/prices.test.ts:185`); M5_AT_018 (`tests/acceptance/M5/stock-dashboard.test.ts:106`); M6_AT_041 (`tests/acceptance/M6/review-and-stock.test.ts:36`) | low |
+| T-22 | T | TB-1 | a provider wants to sell below cost, so the platform pays the fee | Set a price under cost, or send an order whose payout is negative | Price floor in pricing (`server/services/pricing.ts:67`) and at send (`server/services/orders.ts:77`); DB backstop `ck_orders_payout_nonneg` (`db/migrations/1760000002000_payments-ledger.sql:12`); INV-6 | M5_AT_003 (`tests/acceptance/M5/prices.test.ts:66`); M4_AT_041 (`tests/acceptance/M4/send-order.test.ts:209`); M4_AT_003 (`tests/acceptance/M4/send-order.test.ts:61`) | low |
+| T-23 | I | TB-4 | anyone who sees a patient's email or text wants health details | Read items or amounts from the order notice | The notice input has no field for items or amounts (`server/services/messaging.ts:9`, :15); the public notice route returns only the practice name and a sign-in link (`server/services/messaging.ts:27`); the token is 32 random bytes (`server/services/messaging.ts:19`); LINV-5 | M4_AT_017 (`tests/acceptance/M4/send-order.test.ts:102`); M4_AT_036 (`tests/acceptance/M4/sign-in.test.ts:65`) | low. A real provider is ⚠ not built (stub only) |
+| T-24 | S | TB-1 | a phisher wants a trusted-looking link that lands on their site | Open redirect through `/sign-in?next=` | `safeNext` keeps only same-site paths (`app/middleware/auth.global.ts:11`) | unit: `tests/unit/session.test.ts:325`. ⚠ no AT | low |
+| T-25 | D | TB-1 | anyone on the internet wants to slow or stop the app | Flood sign-in, pay or read routes | Sign-in and pay limited to 10 per 15 minutes per person and per address (`server/services/session.ts:101`, `server/services/payments.ts:59`); failed stats writes never fail a request (`server/services/request-metrics.ts:72`) | M5_AT_031 (`tests/acceptance/M5/m4-regressions.test.ts:44`); unit (`tests/unit/hardening.test.ts:158`) | med. Read routes have no limit and each counted request writes a stats row (SEC-17, D89). One app instance, no autoscale (HLD TH-3) |
+| T-26 | S | TB-4 | an attacker wants an order marked paid without paying | Fake a "paid" answer from the payment provider | Today the gateway is an in-process stub with no inbound call (`server/services/payment-gateway.ts:34`). Signature check and confirm-by-asking for a real provider: ⚠ not built (HLD TH-10) | ⚠ no test | med once a real provider is added: node-forge's forged-signature advisory is accepted only while nothing verifies signatures (SEC-2, D49) |
+| T-27 | E, I | TB-5 | someone with the host account or a leaked secret wants everything | Read the database password, deploy bad code, or find a secret in git history | Deploys are human-only (`AGENTS.md`, HLD TH-12). Secret store, private network, database TLS and host two-factor: ⚠ not built in the repo (N3, N6). History scan is a grep heuristic only (CHECKLIST secret scan, 16 false positives) | ⚠ no test | med. Outside the code. No verified gitleaks scan has run on a repo with a public mirror (N4) |
+| T-28 | S | TB-1 | Cerbo's EHR, once it embeds the app, becomes the source of who the patient is | Forge or reuse a launch identity to see another patient's list | Launch-token check: ⚠ not built; framing is blocked today (`nuxt.config.ts:21`) | ⚠ no test | high once embedded, none today (N7) |
+
+## How the threats map to the HLD
+
+| HLD threat | Rows here |
+|---|---|
+| TH-1 session theft | T-14, T-15 |
+| TH-2 price tamper | T-5, T-6 |
+| TH-3 flooding | T-25 |
+| TH-4 open another's order | T-1, T-2, T-3, T-4 |
+| TH-5 ops learn patient identity | T-18 |
+| TH-6 role escalation | T-20 |
+| TH-7 deny a change | T-11 |
+| TH-8 bug edits paid money | T-9, T-10 |
+| TH-9 database password leak | T-27 |
+| TH-10 fake provider answer | T-26 |
+| TH-11 health detail in notice | T-23 |
+| TH-12 host account | T-27 |
+
+## Gaps, ranked (⚠ rows)
+
+Worst first. "Not built" means the repo has no defence; "no test" means the defence exists but nothing proves it.
+
+1. **T-28 embed identity (not built).** No launch-token check exists. Harmless today because framing is blocked
+   (`nuxt.config.ts:21`). It becomes the main trust boundary the day the app is embedded in Cerbo (N7).
+2. **T-27 host and secrets (not built, no test).** Secret store, private database network, database TLS and
+   host two-factor live outside the repo (N3, N6). No verified history scan has run (N4).
+3. **T-26 real payment provider (not built, no test).** Signature verification and confirm-by-asking do not
+   exist yet. Must ship with the first real provider, together with the D49 trigger for node-forge.
+4. **T-13 cost/fee leak to a patient (no test).** The response shapes hold today, but no test asserts that
+   cost, payout or fee are absent from the patient's order view or receipt. A new field would leak silently.
+5. **T-5 forged price field (no test).** The strict schema refuses extra fields, but no test sends one.
+6. **T-16 cross-site form post (no AT).** Defended in depth; only unit-tested for sign-in. No acceptance test
+   posts a form or a cross-origin request at a write route.
+7. **T-17 clickjacking (no AT).** Header is unit-tested from config only; the live header is unchecked (N1).
+8. **T-24 open redirect (no AT).** `safeNext` is unit-tested only.
+
+Medium residual risks with tests in place: T-9 and T-11 (owner role and live grants unchecked, N10),
+T-15 (shared demo password, Q2; proxy address, N2), T-25 (read routes unlimited, SEC-17).
